// The crested lizard hand puppet with a Turing pattern grown over its skin: red spots on the
// scales, simulated over the head and the jaw, in up to nine filaments. The part's Pattern knobs
// regrow it (spots, stripes, a labyrinth; its scale, seed and steps).
use mod.fab.*

script("lizard_puppet.cad.splash", params: {pattern: 1})

// In four filaments the spots are in the mouth's red, on the other nozzle from the scales: the
// skin switches heads on every layer but swaps no filament. Spots in the slits' dark would trade
// nozzles with the red on most layers, more than doubling the purge.
color("Teal", rgb: #x1a9999)
color("Red", rgb: #xb30d1f)
color("White", rgb: #xf2f2eb)
color("Dark", rgb: #x140f1a)
color("Blue", rgb: #x1f4dbf)
color("Yellow", rgb: #xf7cc26)
color("Pink", rgb: #xf28099)
color("Orange", rgb: #xf2731a)
color("Purple", rgb: #x7333a6)

place("lizard_puppet", object: "Lizard puppet", at: [175mm 160mm], rotate: 135°, name: "Turing lizard", color: "Teal")
